# Build context allowlist for workers/media-worker/Dockerfile (context = repo root).
# Everything is excluded, then only the Python workspace subset the worker image needs is
# re-included — keeps node_modules/.git/apps out of the daemon upload (hundreds of MB).
#
# Docker semantics: after `*` excludes everything, `!packages` re-includes the DIRECTORY ENTRY but
# NOT its contents — the build would copy empty dirs and `uv sync` would fail (CodeX #61 P1). So the
# re-includes must recurse (`!packages/**`); the heavy re-excludes come AFTER (last match wins).
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!packages
!packages/**
!workers
!workers/**
# Re-exclude heavy/unneeded paths within the re-included trees (order: after the !includes above).
packages/schemas/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/.pytest_cache
